---
import MarketingLayout from '@/layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import CampaignSectionHeading from '@/components/campaign/CampaignSectionHeading.astro';
import CampaignThemeImage from '@/components/campaign/CampaignThemeImage.astro';
import MarketingPackGrid from '@/components/marketing/MarketingPackGrid.astro';
import Callout from '@/components/Callout.astro';
import { marketingTasks } from '@/data/marketing/tasks.mjs';
---
<MarketingLayout title="Marketing" description="Ready-to-use emails, LinkedIn campaigns and presentations to help your network contribute to OPDA’s working groups." landing>
  <div class="marketing-pack-heading">
    <h1>Marketing</h1>
    <p class="lead">Help the people in your network bring their experience to better property information. Find an invitation, presentation or campaign you can adapt and share.</p>
  </div>

  <section aria-labelledby="member-sharing">
    <CampaignSectionHeading eyebrow="For organisations, networks and communities" title="Bring your members’ experience into the work." id="member-sharing" size="panel" align="start">
      <Fragment slot="aside">
        <CampaignThemeImage lightSrc="/images/join/set-3/motivation-landscape-light.webp" darkSrc="/images/join/set-3/motivation-landscape-dark.webp" alt="People bringing different professional experiences to a shared property project." width={1536} height={512} loading="eager" />
      </Fragment>
    </CampaignSectionHeading>
    <p>Professional bodies, industry networks and community groups can reach people whose knowledge belongs in this work. Our packs give you a member-facing invitation, LinkedIn posts and a short presentation. Choose a relevant field, add your own introduction and share through your usual channels.</p>
    <div class="marketing-actions">
      <a class="btn" href="/marketing/share-with-members">Get a member-sharing pack</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/marketing/invite-someone">Ask an organisation to share</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="sharing-tasks">
    <CampaignSectionHeading eyebrow="Start with what you want to do" title="The right material for the conversation." id="sharing-tasks" size="panel" />
    <div class="marketing-task-grid">
      {marketingTasks.map((task) => <a class="marketing-task-card" href={`/marketing/${task.id}`}>
        <span class="marketing-eyebrow">{task.eyebrow}</span>
        <h3>{task.title}</h3>
        <p>{task.description}</p>
        <span class="marketing-pack-card__action">{task.action} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span>
      </a>)}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="campaign-packs">
    <CampaignSectionHeading eyebrow="Relevant to your audience" title="One complete pack for each part of the journey." id="campaign-packs" size="panel" />
    <p>Use the general pack for a mixed audience, or choose a pack with examples from a particular field. Each includes three email versions, an OPDA and an organisation LinkedIn sequence, artwork, a short slide deck and a one-page overview.</p>
    <MarketingPackGrid />
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="simple-handoff">
    <CampaignSectionHeading eyebrow="From a useful contact to a useful contribution" title="A simple handoff, through trusted relationships." id="simple-handoff" size="panel" />
    <ol class="marketing-steps">
      <li><h3>1. Choose and adapt</h3><p>Pick a pack for the audience. Use the version written for the person or organisation sending it.</p></li>
      <li><h3>2. Share through your channels</h3><p>Send an email, include a newsletter item, post on LinkedIn or introduce the opportunity at a meeting.</p></li>
      <li><h3>3. Let people decide</h3><p>Interested people explore the working groups and register directly with OPDA. Each expression of interest is reviewed.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <Callout title="Your relationship with your members stays yours" tone="method">
      <p>OPDA does not need your membership list. Share the opportunity yourself and let individuals choose whether to register. These tools prepare materials; they do not send emails or publish posts.</p>
    </Callout>
  </section>
</MarketingLayout>
